# Quebit API Test Collection
# Use with VS Code REST Client extension or similar HTTP client tools.
# Variables can be overridden per-environment.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Health Check
GET {{host}}/healthz

### Create Payment
POST {{host}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "order-12345",
  "amount": 5000,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Create Payment (idempotent replay — same key)
POST {{host}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "order-12345",
  "amount": 5000,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Create Payment (high value — routes to critical queue)
POST {{host}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "order-99999",
  "amount": 50000,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### Create Payment (low value — routes to low queue)
POST {{host}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "order-small-1",
  "amount": 500,
  "currency": "GBP"
}

### Get Payment by ID
# Replace the UUID with an actual payment ID from a create response
GET {{host}}/v1/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Retry Failed Payment
# Replace the UUID with an actual payment ID that is in failed_final state
POST {{host}}/v1/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/retry

### Validation Error — Missing fields
POST {{host}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Validation Error — Negative amount
POST {{host}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idempotency_key": "bad-amount",
  "amount": -100,
  "currency": "USD"
}

### Bad Request — Invalid JSON
POST {{host}}/v1/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{this is not valid json}

### Not Found — Bad UUID
GET {{host}}/v1/payments/not-a-uuid
